

--> @OpenAPIDefinition
    @OpenAPIDefinition is used to define global metadata for the entire API documentation.
    Instead of repeating information for every endpoint, this annotation provides:
    API name
    Version
    Description
    Server/environment details


--> What It Represents in Swagger UI
    Information defined using @OpenAPIDefinition appears at the top of Swagger UI, acting like a cover page for the API.
    It gives consumers immediate clarity about:
    What this API is for
    Which version they are using
    Which environment they are connected to


--> Why It Is Important
    Standardizes documentation across services
    Helps version control APIs
    Essential for enterprise and production-grade systems
    Useful when the same API is deployed across multiple environments (dev, QA, prod)


